# Vault index for Claude

## In every session

- Answer in short, plain English. Lead with the answer. The user, or their own instructions, may
  say otherwise.
- Create a new personal skill or agent in this vault, not straight in `~/.claude/skills` or
  `~/.claude/agents`, unless the user names another place. The vault is
  `~/.claude/second-brain-vault/`.
- Add it by the steps under `## Adding a skill or agent` in the vault's `claude/README.md`.
  Claude Code loads it only after `second-brain link --apply`.
- A rule about one project goes under `## Rules` in `<Path>/claude/README.md`, or in its
  subproject's note. Only a rule for every project goes in `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Unsure which: ask.
- Call a plugin skill or agent for its work, even when the helper alone could answer. Skills:
  `story-tracker` for any question or change on a ticket (where it stands, a standup, an
  update), `sprint` runs a sprint, `vault-setup` sets up the vault or a project, `vault-doctor`
  checks them. Agents: `scrum-master` for the sprint cadence,
  `docs-keeper` for docs that follow the code and for a ticket marked done.
- Write a pull request description in the format of
  `~/.claude/second-brain-vault/claude/pull-request.md`; a project's own
  `<Path>/claude/pull-request.md` wins.

## Working on a project or on notes

- When a request belongs to a project below, read `<Path>/README.md`, then `<Path>/claude/README.md`
  and the `claude/subprojects/<name>.md` that `second-brain context` names, before anything else.
- Before reading or writing notes, run `second-brain conventions` and follow it. The full note is
  `~/.claude/second-brain-vault/obsidian-conventions.md`.

## Rules for notes that most often go wrong

- Find and read notes with the helper, never with grep, cat or sed on vault files:
  `second-brain find`, `search` (also for related notes before a decision), `task head`, then
  `outline` and a ranged read, and a whole note last.
- A task note is always `<project>/tasks/<TICKET-ID>/README.md`, under `tasks/archive/<YYYY>/`
  once archived.
- Never file a task note inside the topic it is about. Tie it to the topic with a tag that is the
  folder path, lowercased, and to its subproject with the `subproject` property.
- A bare `[[Alias]]` does not resolve. Links carry a path:
  `[[<vault path or unique file name>|<alias>]]`.
- Move and rename notes with `second-brain move` and `second-brain rename`, never `mv`.
- Frontmatter is the truth. Read a status from the `status` property, never from prose.
- Ticket text is never written freehand. Use `story-tracker`: it opens with `*As a* <persona>,` /
  `*I need to* ...,` / `*so that* ...` and holds at most 4 acceptance criteria.

